mantle rm486
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_cedric_ashcot
title the folding hill
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk folds_old_maps_into_steps_to_show_the_slope
likes honey_cakes old_tales old_maps first_warm_day
dislikes rats crowds
fears a_map_without_a_key a_queue_at_a_narrow_door
hopes a_walk_whose_map_is_exact a_letter_full_of_vineyard_weather
topics travel +0.5 newcomer +0.4 lore +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# folds a street plan into steps and freely points out every mistake in the drawing, especially the errors of the most recent revision.

words
oath! = Ink on a honey cake | A fold across the compass
saying! = A flat street on paper can still take your breath | Turn the sheet before you turn a walker
longrise = two strides of stair | my uphill double step
shortfall = a single inward fold | the false valley
roofmark = a tiny black angle | an ink roof
softbend = the old soft crease | the line of least resistance
goodeye = my uppermost lookout | a space on the high landing
caketooth = the sugary corner | that honeyed edge
trailspot = a spot of sticky yellow | a honey mark
vinehand = a hand from the vineyards | the slanting country script
signhook = a square of bent iron | my door bracket
doorstop = the wedge under the leaf | a firm oak toe

any
opinion city for 1 : There's a different town visible from each high landing, and each view answers to the same honest address.
opinion festivals for 1 : Put the music within earshot of an uncrowded step. I'd happily pay the fiddler afterwards.
opinion merchants against 1 : A seller who would conceal a broken hinge is a poor ornament to a shop of any description. I prefer my hinges visible.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A wolf who asks why the lanes curve deserves the best account of the hill I can unfold.
opinion strangers for 1 : The unfamiliar face in a doorway may have a perfectly familiar reason for coming inside.
opinion sump against 1 : I find the low market rather too close about my shoulders. Up here I can usually see my next ten paces.

grown
line greet : Welcome to the high margin of my little plan.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You're new to my map. Come and locate yourself.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : The first light's found my highest fold already.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : There remains a bright landing for your feet.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Hold the map by its blank corner for me.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come and occupy a respectable place on my hill.
line again.open : Familiar feet on a fresh fold.
line greet.return : A clear greeting came uphill from you.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I've room on this landing for a familiar voice.
line farewell : May the ink agree with the hill you actually climb.
line farewell.return : I'll leave your road unfolded for a while.
line react.news : Whereabouts would you put that account on a street plan?
line react.news.new : That deserves a fresh scrap of paper.
line react.news.known : There's already a mark for that occurrence.
line react.news.doubt : Were the distances measured from an actual doorstep?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd take quiet company and a cake to the household.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : There's something I could whistle up two flights of stairs.
line answer.how : Comfortable, and curious about a turn I haven't drawn yet.
line ask.how : What view did the day present from your stair?
line sympathise : I'd leave a seat vacant for the load you brought along.
line decline : I owe my attention to this doorway before I take another turn.
line accept_decline : I'll find a separate occasion for that request of mine.
line thank : My papers have acquired a considerably better direction.
line preclose : I've one crease still wanting my thumb.
line ack : Quite legible.

scene hill
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Three folds can give this hill a tolerably convincing slope.
b : Why bother with a slope in paper? | Can a real turn be folded?
a : A visitor feels the cost of a shortcut in boot leather. A short steep climb is a significant sort of distance. | I ink the turn after folding. Otherwise some perfectly useful corner will run across a roof.

scene door
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shop door should give a caller some idea how far it will open.
b : What could make that doubtful? | Can you make it more welcoming?
a : A large display set just inside the sweep. I try the full arc before declaring the entrance quite ready. | A space to pause saves a caller the embarrassment of stepping directly into someone else's purchase.

scene stairs
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I climb the long flights in pairs of treads.
b : How do you finish an odd flight? | Would you descend in pairs?
a : I save the single tread for last. It gives my breathing a little time to acquire better manners. | Certainly not. Coming down I find a modest single tread entirely sufficient.

scene maps
when topic=lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My favourite plan gives a road to a patch of empty hillside.
b : Doesn't a fictitious road spoil it? | Would you mend the mistake?
a : It improves the conversation considerably. I wouldn't give the sheet to a traveller without first describing its curious ambition. | In a different colour, with room for the reader to appreciate the artist's original optimism.

scene honey
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lick my sticky fingertips clean before unfolding any valuable sheet.
b : Wouldn't a cloth do? | Is the paper really valuable?
a : It could. The cloth would then enjoy an advantage which belongs by right to the purchaser of the cake. | Some of it only to me. That's precisely the sort of value a seller has trouble adequately accounting for.

scene letter
when topic=family
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Vineyard correspondence has room for the week's weather in four crooked lines.
b : Do you want a long letter? | What makes the lines crooked?
a : A plain detail is enough. A wet boot sitting beside a vine tells me rather more than an entire page of formal regards. | The slope of the writing, I hope. I'd be grieved to think a relation had been carrying ink up my paper hill.

scene tales
when topic=memories self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old tale deserves to get its original turns, even when everybody can see the finish.
b : Would you correct a teller? | What makes a turn worth the wait?
a : Only by invitation. On my own hearth I admit to giving the missing bit after the teller's had a cake. | A door described early which opens upon the last page. I want to discover where the teller has left its hinges.

scene spring
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell the first warm day by how long I linger over an unnecessary stair.
b : Are there truly unnecessary stairs? | How long do you linger?
a : For getting directly along my assigned way, yes. For seeing the roofs take the light, none whatsoever. | Until a second detail becomes visible where before I'd seen only a patch of brown tiles.

scene rats
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gnawed corner of a plan may make two formerly distant streets appear uncommonly close.
b : A rat did that? | Would you keep the sheet?
a : I'd hesitate to authenticate the artist. There were tooth marks and a suspicious absence of interest in the inked section. | With a replacement corner of different paper. The damage is part of its travels now.

scene crowd
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A festival seen from one landing up has the advantage of some breathing space between tunes.
b : Can you see the players? | Won't you miss joining in?
a : Their bows mostly. An excellent machine, a bow rising and falling above all those occupied ears. | I can join in by putting a copper in the collection. My singing would hardly be a contribution of the same order.

scene heights
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A walker below sees our high walls. I see eight completely different ways of hanging a gate.
b : Which pleases you most? | Eight on one walk?
a : The one which opens without pushing a caller off a step. I'm content with grace in the metal after that's been attended to. | On a sufficiently slow walk. It is entirely possible to climb quickly and then look for a considerable interval.

scene forge
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# a door can frame a great deal of interesting iron.
b : What catches your eye? | Would you sell me a hinge?
a : The curves where a smith thought about a moving joint before putting an ornament on it. I shall examine which idea came first. | Ask me for its price at the proper time. I'd want the weight of your gate before pronouncing upon its hinge.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I should like to set a sheet before #self.friend# and see which place gets drawn first.
b : What would your own first mark be? | Would you correct it?
a : My next stair, probably. A friend might begin with a quite different stone and get just as good a town. | I should ask about it. I'm drawing the view from a friend's doorstep, which will hardly resemble mine.

scene price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I will say plainly when a handsome object won't do a caller's job.
b : Even if it costs you a sale? | What will you show instead?
a : A bad purchase tends to become my business again. I might as well start by showing a more suitable article. | Something chosen after hearing what has to turn, swing or hold still. All three have demanding opinions on fit.

scene rain
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet crease can turn a copied street into a fine black stream.
b : Would you rub it dry? | What becomes of the stream?
a : Never. A little time laid open in moving air costs less than a sound copy. | I ink a correction in its margin. Nobody should mistake an afternoon shower for a change to our harbour.

scene guest
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A visitor once asked for the quickest route and then showed me a boot with a loose sole.
b : Did you change your directions? | What mark shows the flatter road?
a : Immediately. The flatter road is considerably quicker when half your boot has its own ideas about which way to turn. | Two little bars for the steep part, and a single sweeping arrow for the longer way that boot could reasonably attempt.

scene quiet
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A map in poor light is mostly an account of old creases.
b : Can you use it like that? | Is the ink actually disappearing?
a : Only my own. I remember enough to supply the streets a candle's elected to leave out. | Nowhere, happily. By morning it's willing to give evidence again without putting up its price.

story hingeline [topic=work self.job=merchant]
  : I opened a folded plan across a shop threshold and tried to put a dot where I stood.
  : My finger followed the swing of the door instead and drew most of a black circle.
  b : Did it ruin the place?
  : I wrote a note on the arc. It became the only street plan I have ever owned which showed a door opening to welcome its reader.

story cakebend [topic=food]
  : A speck of honey once kept two folds of my plan firmly joined for a week.
  : I was quite unreasonably cross at how small the town had become before the reason presented itself.
  b : How did you part them?
  : Very slowly indeed. Both streets came out whole and for a few days the hill smelled much better than usual.

story twostairs [topic=travel]
  : I climbed an unfamiliar flight in double steps with a sheet tucked into my collar.
  : At the landing I discovered a small chalk arrow drawn level with my kneecap.
  b : Where did it lead?
  : Downwards to a lower view I'd missed entirely by being so splendidly efficient about going up.

rule @door
when concept=bark self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Allow the door its full quarter turn. | New iron on the inside display.

rule @cake
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A clean finger for a clean plan. | Save that honeyed corner till the ink is dry.

rule @stairs
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One stride for two old treads. | First light on the folded summit.

rule @crowd
when concept=bark self.dislikes=crowds
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's air up on that landing. | The bows are visible above the heads.
dlg resident.hub : Choose a fold and we can discuss the hill it claims to represent.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I recognise that approach, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I will keep my paper open with the marks in plain view.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : A candle will show one fold at a time. We have just enough light for that.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I'd have each caller see how far the door will swing before buying the hinge.
dlg resident.job : I'm usually near an entrance with an answer about the climb.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : There's a new mark on the street plan. #world.news#.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : The doorway's clear for a caller to look over the iron offered today.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : An empty display behind me today. I can still answer a question about a fitting.
dlg shop.prices : Tell me which iron piece has caught your eye and I'll give its price plainly.
dlg shop.bye : I hope the fitting does exactly what the door requires.
dlg resident.bye : Give the long route its due if your boot is loose.

graft @mapfold resident.hub
choice Why does that map stand up? -> mapfold
node mapfold
say Each crease adds a little of the height a flat draughtsman left out. See how short that road looks until I lift the paper beneath it.
choice How would you show my own walk? -> mapfold_more
choice Lay the hill open. -> hub
node mapfold_more
say Put a finger where your journey began. I will raise the intervening folds, and your knees may be able to supply the rest of the information.
choice Lay the hill open. -> hub
choice Leave by the level street. -> bye
